  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:conditional-frontier",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "The claimed conditional frontier does not hold over \\(\\mathcal M_{N,T,\\mathbf n}\\) as currently defined. There are admissible fixed class parameters, a scalar specialization, a growth array, two laws in the class, and positive-probability exact-design rectangles on which \\(g_{1T}(z_0)<1\\) and \\(R_D\\to0\\), but \\(\\mathbb E[(\\widehat\\tau-\\tau(z_0))^2\\mid z_0,(X_t)]\\) is bounded away from zero under one law. Hence no fixed finite \\(C\\) can satisfy the displayed upper bound for \\(\\widehat\\tau\\), and the three-sided frontier is false without an event-outcome conditional-centering restriction relative to the realized design.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "M",
      "N",
      "T",
      "n_s",
      "n_vec",
      "g_sT",
      "z_0",
      "R_D",
      "hat_tau",
      "tau",
      "C"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:panel-model-class",
      "def:target",
      "def:conditional-rate",
      "def:frontier-estimator",
      "lem:common-design-shock-obstruction"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Apply \\texttt{lem:common-design-shock-obstruction}.  On every design array in the positive-probability rectangle \\(\\mathcal D_n\\), the lemma gives \\(g_{1T}(z_0)<1\\), \\(R_D=n^{-1}\\to0\\), and\n\\[\n \\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal M_{N,T,\\mathbf n}}\n \\mathbb E_P[(\\widehat\\tau-\\tau(z_0))^2\\mid z_0,(X_t)]\n \\ge {\\Delta^2\\over4}+o(1).\n\\]\nFor any fixed finite \\(C\\), the right side of the claimed estimator upper bound, \\(CR_D=C/n\\), tends to zero.  Thus that upper bound is false.  Since it is one inequality in the asserted three-sided chain, the claimed conditional frontier is false as stated.  The witness satisfies all frozen class conditions; the missing premise is a restriction such as \\(E[B_{si}^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\mid z_0,(X_{uv})]=\\mu_{1s}(z_0)\\), which is not present in the frozen core and is not used here as an assumption.",
